{# A trigger plus an `option_list` popover, in three variants over ONE component.

   `facet`  — a labeled, full-width filter; selection and submission use the same handlers.
   `field`  — the PROPERTY PILL of an add or edit surface: a small rounded outline
              chip of icon + text, sitting in the `property_row` beneath the text
              lines. It carries hidden inputs and writes when the form does.
              `prominent` makes ONE pill of a row visually heavier, for a property
              that is not a peer of the others — on the create dialog that is
              `workflow`, which decides the ticket's whole state flow and cannot be
              changed cheaply afterwards, so it leads the row and is marked. Linear
              does the same for `status`: first in the row, and the only pill that
              carries its own state colour. It is a PROP rather than a class a scene
              applies, so prominence is a declared property of the field rather than
              styling that happens to have been pasted in one place.
   `inline` — the displayed VALUE is the trigger and there are no hidden inputs,
              because for a reversible field the pick is the write. Only
              reversible fields may use it; `state` may not, because a transition
              is confirmed and a control that writes on pick cannot carry a
              confirmation (designbook/design-system/action-pattern.md).
              With `autosave` the pick submits the enclosing form, and `status`
              says beside the value what the last write did: "Saved", or the
              error that refused it (`invalid`).

   One component, not two: the ticket this implements asked for ONE agreed
   pattern, and two components that happen to look alike is how that requirement
   is quietly lost. The two variants are now one grammar at two sizes — a pill in
   a dialog, the bare value on a detail screen.

   THE PILL CARRIES ITS OWN NAME, twice over, and both are load-bearing because
   the surface has no visible labels (action-pattern.md, rules 1, 2 and 4):

   - Visibly: the pill shows the FIELD NAME and, once something is set, the VALUE
     BESIDE IT — "Conductor · cw-framework", not "cw-framework" (C17). The pill
     used to swap one string for the other, and the human read the result at the
     second review gate: a bare value cannot be told apart from the field's own
     name, so a pill reading "backend, ui" could as easily have been a field
     called that. An unset pill still reads "Conductor" alone, which is the
     answer to what the control is for.
     The INLINE variant keeps a border and a trailing chevron at rest, so it
     reads as editable without a hover.
     The INLINE variant does NOT repeat the field name: it sits in a labelled
     `meta_row`, so repeating it there would put the same word twice on one line
     and make the value look like a second field. The `aria-label` names the
     field in both variants regardless.
   - Accessibly: `aria-label` in Linear's state-carrying form — "Change conductor.
     Currently no conductor is set." It is rendered for BOTH variants, never
     gated on one, because with the `<label>` gone it is the only name the control
     has. A caller should pass `aria_label`; when it does not, one is derived from
     `label` and the selected labels so the name can never come out empty.

   MULTI-SELECT IS RENDERED, NOT ONLY SUBMITTED (C18). `multiple` used to do
   exactly one thing — append `[]` to the hidden input name — and it was the only
   prop here with no description, which is the tell that nothing had decided what
   it should look like. Several values now render as the FIRST value plus a `+N`
   count, which is what fits in a 28px pill without wrapping the row it sits in.
   Nothing about the panel changes: `option_list` already owns multi-select
   properly (`aria-multiselectable`, a marker box per row), so this composes with
   it and deliberately duplicates none of it.

   AN OVER-LONG VALUE HAS A DEFINED TREATMENT (C19), and truncation is no longer
   the whole of it. The value is bounded (`max-w-…` plus `truncate`) so one long
   term cannot stretch a pill row off the surface, and the full text stays
   reachable two ways: in the `title` attribute, and in the state-carrying
   `aria-label` — which is not decoration here, it is the control's only name.
   The panel is allowed to grow with its content up to a ceiling as well, so a
   long term is legible where it is actually chosen rather than only in a
   tooltip.

   `role="combobox"` + `aria-haspopup="listbox"` say what the pill IS. The cost is
   named in the spec (D14): a combobox owes its user focus management,
   `aria-activedescendant` and Escape. Opening moves focus into the panel, arrows
   move between rows, Enter or Space picks and Escape closes; focus moves to the
   rows themselves rather than through `aria-activedescendant`.

   The open state is `aria-expanded` on the trigger plus `hidden` on the panel,
   both rendered from the `open` prop — accessible attributes, never a CSS class,
   which is what makes the states readable with JavaScript disabled.
   `option_picker.src.js` is an Alpine component (`Alpine.data('optionPicker')`) that
   BINDS exactly those two attributes at runtime and is purely additive; nothing
   here depends on it. Alpine initialises any subtree inserted into the document
   by itself, without waiting for an event, which is what makes it survive an
   htmx swap.

   CLEARING IS NOT HERE. It is the first row of the `option_list` in the panel,
   which is where a row of a listbox has to live; this component used to own a
   clear button above the list and no longer does.

   The panel has a FLOOR width rather than hugging its content freely, so it does not jump between
   sizes from one field to the next; it may grow to a ceiling for long option labels, which is the
   panel half of C19 — a term the operator cannot read in the list it is chosen from is not made
   readable by a tooltip on the trigger. The search row sits at the TOP, above the rows, where Linear
   puts it; and the selected marker sits on the RIGHT of each row (see option_list), so every row's
   text starts at the same left edge.

   `searchable` is a BOUNDARY, not a feature: it renders the search input the
   parent field needs and filters nothing. Agreeing the placement now is what
   keeps the ticket that gives that field real candidates from restructuring the
   control. Group headers inside the panel are the same kind of boundary — the
   grammar permits them, and nothing here fakes them. #}
{% set picker_id = id|default('bakers-option-picker') %}
{% set panel = panel_id|default(picker_id ~ '__panel') %}
{% set is_inline = variant|default('field') == 'inline' %}
{#- The selected labels as a LIST, which is what C18's `+N` counts and what C19 puts in the title.
    `value_labels` is the multi form; `value_label` stays supported for a single value, so every
    caller written before this change keeps rendering exactly as it did — a caller that hands over a
    pre-joined string simply gets one long value instead of a count, which is the old behaviour
    rather than a broken one. #}
{% set value_list = value_labels|default(value_label is not empty ? [value_label] : []) %}
{% set has_value = value_list is not empty %}
{% set field_name = label|default('') %}
{% set all_values = value_list|join(', ') %}
{#- HOW MANY VALUES, counted over the list's KEYS and never with `|length` on the list itself. That is
    a measured constraint rather than a preference. In the Storybook renderer (Twing in the browser)
    `|length` on these prop arrays returns the length of their STRING coercion — a two-value field
    rendered `+12`, because `String(['coding','review'])` is 13 characters long — and `loop.last` is
    wrong for the same reason: it fires on the FIRST iteration, so a loop-counted version printed no
    count at all. `|keys`, `|first`, `|join` and plain iteration all behave correctly on the same
    value, and `|keys|length` measures a list Twig built itself. Verified in the browser renderer on a
    four-value field: `|keys|length` 4, `|length` 56, `loop.last` on iteration 1. #}
{% set value_count = has_value ? value_list|keys|length : 0 %}
{% set first_value = has_value ? value_list|first : '' %}
{#- The full text, unbounded and untruncated, for the `title` attribute: the value alone on an inline
    control (the row already names the field) and "Field: value, value" on a pill. When nothing is
    set the title is the field name, so hovering an empty control still answers what it is for. #}
{% set trigger_title = has_value
  ? (is_inline or field_name is empty ? all_values : field_name ~ ': ' ~ all_values)
  : field_name %}
{#- The search box needs its OWN accessible name. It is a third text-entry control, and it shipped
    with nothing but a placeholder until the human read the DOM and found it — the same weak name the
    text lines are forbidden from relying on. `form_input` is an existing component and cannot be modified
    (C14), so the name is passed in through `attributes`, which is what that passthrough is for.
    Derived from the placeholder when a caller gives no `search_label`, so it is never empty. #}
{% set search_aria = search_label|default(search_placeholder)|default('Search') %}
{#- Derived from the FULL list, never from the truncated first value: the accessible name is the one
    place the whole selection has to be available even when the pill shows "backend +2". #}
{% set trigger_aria = aria_label|default(
  'Change ' ~ (label|default('value')) ~ '. '
  ~ (has_value ? 'Currently ' ~ all_values ~ '.' : 'Nothing is set.')
) %}
{% set is_facet = variant == 'facet' %}
{% set use_chips = selected_chips|default(false) %}
{% set chip_items = selected|default([]) %}
{#- SERVER SEARCH. With `search_url` the search box stops filtering what was rendered and asks the
    server instead: htmx GETs the URL with the typed text as `q` and swaps the returned option_list
    rows into the panel, so a candidate beyond the first rendered page is still found. Without it
    nothing below changes. `hx-select` and `hx-select-oob` are unset so a dialog form's inherited
    selectors cannot filter the returned rows away. #}
{% set search_input_attributes = create_attribute()
  .setAttribute('data-option-picker-search', true)
  .setAttribute('data-bef-auto-submit-exclude', true)
  .setAttribute('x-model', 'query')
  .setAttribute('@input', 'filter()')
  .setAttribute('aria-label', search_aria) %}
{% if search_url %}
  {% set search_input_attributes = search_input_attributes
    .setAttribute('name', 'q')
    .setAttribute('hx-get', search_url)
    .setAttribute('hx-trigger', 'input changed delay:250ms, search')
    .setAttribute('hx-target', '#' ~ panel ~ '__rows')
    .setAttribute('hx-swap', 'innerHTML')
    .setAttribute('hx-sync', 'this:replace')
    .setAttribute('hx-select', 'unset')
    .setAttribute('hx-select-oob', 'unset') %}
{% endif %}
{% set pill_classes = ['inline-flex',
  'items-center', 'gap-1.5', 'h-control', 'px-2.5', 'rounded-full', 'text-left',
  'whitespace-nowrap', 'cursor-pointer', 'border', 'focus:border-primary', 'focus-visible:outline-2', 'focus-visible:outline-offset-2', 'focus-visible:outline-focus-ring'] %}
{% set pill_weight = prominent
  ? ['bg-primary/10', 'border-primary/45', 'text-primary',
     'text-label', 'hover:bg-primary/15']
  : ['bg-app', 'border-control-border', 'text-text', 'text-meta', 'hover:bg-surface-3'] %}
{#- C19's bound on the displayed value, written as two LITERAL class strings rather than one
    interpolated arbitrary value: Tailwind generates a utility only when the candidate appears
    verbatim in the source it scans, so `max-w-[{{ … }}]` would compile to nothing at all and the
    bound would silently not exist. The inline control may run wider because it sits alone on a rail
    row; a pill shares a wrapping row with its peers and may not. #}
{% set value_bound = is_inline ? 'max-w-60' : 'max-w-40' %}
{#- `align-middle` keeps the inline trigger's line at its own 24px. On the text baseline,
    a trigger without an icon grew its line by the font's descent: a 32px row became 35px. #}
{% set trigger_classes = is_inline
  ? ['inline-flex', 'items-center', 'align-middle', 'gap-1.5', 'h-6', 'px-1.5',
     'bg-app', 'border', 'border-control-border', 'rounded-xs', 'text-body',
     'text-text', 'text-left', 'cursor-pointer', 'hover:bg-surface-3',
     'focus:border-primary', 'focus-visible:outline-2', 'focus-visible:outline-offset-2', 'focus-visible:outline-focus-ring']
  : pill_classes|merge(pill_weight) %}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['relative', use_chips ? 'inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5' : (is_facet ? 'block w-full' : 'inline-block')]) }}
  data-option-picker
  data-option-picker-label="{{ field_name }}"
  {%- if use_chips %} data-option-picker-selected-chips{% endif %}
  {#- Which variant this is, for the disclosure handler: the inline variant
      never writes a hidden input (see above), and `name` alone cannot say so
      — `table.twig`'s `kind == 'picker'` cell sets both `variant: 'inline'`
      AND `name` on the same instance. #}
  data-option-picker-variant="{{ is_inline ? 'inline' : (is_facet ? 'facet' : 'field') }}"
  {%- if search_url %} data-option-picker-remote{% endif %}
  {%- if name %} data-option-picker-name="{{ name }}"{% endif %}
  x-data="optionPicker()"
  {#- AUTOSAVE: a pick that leaves the checked options different from what the server
      rendered submits the enclosing form, and the answer replaces the form. So the
      rendered selection is never updated here: an unchanged pick or a dismissal writes
      nothing, a pick after a failed request submits again, and htmx drops a submit
      while one is in flight. The pick clears the previous status. #}
  {%- if autosave %}
  data-option-picker-autosave
  x-init="$el.dataset.rendered = [...$el.querySelectorAll('[data-option-picker-panel] input:checked')].map((i) => i.value).join()"
  @bakers-picker-picked="[...$el.querySelectorAll('[data-option-picker-panel] input:checked')].map((i) => i.value).join() === $el.dataset.rendered || ($el.querySelector('[data-picker-part=status]')?.replaceChildren(), $el.closest('form')?.requestSubmit())"
  {%- endif %}
  {#- These four replace the document-level handlers the behaviour used to
      register once on `body`: one picker owns its own dismissal and its own
      re-placement, rather than a single listener sweeping every picker. #}
  @keydown.escape="if (open) { $event.stopPropagation(); dismiss(); }"
  @click.outside="close()"
  @resize.window="reposition()"
  @scroll.window.capture="reposition()">
  {% if is_facet %}<label for="{{ picker_id }}" class="block pb-1.5 text-label text-text-light">{{ field_name }}</label>{% endif %}
  {% set trigger_classes = is_facet ? ['flex', 'items-center', 'gap-inline', 'w-full', 'min-h-control', 'px-inline', 'py-inline', 'rounded-xs', 'border', 'border-control-border', 'bg-app', 'text-body', 'text-text', 'text-left', 'cursor-pointer', 'focus-visible:outline-2', 'focus-visible:outline-offset-2', 'focus-visible:outline-focus-ring'] : trigger_classes %}
  <button type="button"{{ create_attribute().addClass(trigger_classes) }}
    id="{{ picker_id }}"
    data-option-picker-trigger
    x-ref="trigger"
    @click="toggle()"
    :aria-expanded="open ? 'true' : 'false'"
    role="combobox"
    aria-haspopup="listbox"
    aria-expanded="{{ open ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
    aria-controls="{{ panel }}"
    aria-label="{{ trigger_aria }}"
    {%- if autosave %} aria-describedby="{{ picker_id }}__status"{% endif %}
    {%- if invalid %} aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}
    title="{{ trigger_title }}">
    {%- if icon and not is_facet %}<span data-picker-part="icon" class="shrink-0 {{ prominent ? 'text-primary' : 'text-text-light' }}">{{ include('bb_theme:icon', { name: icon, size: 'sm' }, with_context = false) }}</span>{% endif %}
    {#- The field name. On a pill it is always rendered — beside the value when one is set (C17), and
        alone when none is. On the inline variant it is left out, because that control sits in a
        labelled row and the same word twice on one line reads as two fields. #}
    {%- if field_name is not empty and not is_inline and not is_facet %}
    <span data-picker-part="field" class="shrink-0 {{ prominent ? 'text-primary/70' : 'text-text-faint' }}">{{ field_name }}</span>
    {%- if has_value and not use_chips %}<span data-picker-part="separator" class="shrink-0 text-text-faint" aria-hidden="true">·</span>{% endif %}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if has_value and not use_chips %}
    <span data-picker-part="value" class="min-w-0 truncate {{ value_bound }}">{{ first_value }}</span>
    {%- if value_count > 1 %}<span data-picker-part="more" class="shrink-0 text-text-light">+{{ value_count - 1 }}</span>{% endif %}
    {%- elseif not has_value and (is_inline or is_facet or field_name is empty) %}
    <span data-picker-part="value" class="min-w-0 truncate text-text-light {{ value_bound }}">{{ is_facet ? 'Any' : (field_name is not empty ? field_name : '—') }}</span>
    {%- endif %}
    {% if is_facet %}<span class="flex flex-1 justify-end">{{ include('bb_theme:icon', { name: 'chevron-down', size: 'sm' }, with_context = false) }}</span>{% endif %}
    {% if is_inline %}<span data-picker-part="chevron" class="shrink-0 text-text-faint" aria-hidden="true">{{ include('bb_theme:icon', { name: 'chevron-down', size: 'sm' }, with_context = false) }}</span>{% endif %}
  </button>
  {%- if use_chips %}
  <span data-option-picker-chips class="inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-inline-xs" {%- if chip_items is empty %} hidden{% endif %}>
    {%- for item in chip_items %}
    <span data-option-picker-chip data-value="{{ item.value }}" class="inline-flex items-center gap-inline-xs h-6 max-w-40 px-1.5 rounded-full border border-control-border bg-app text-meta">
      <span class="min-w-0 truncate" title="{{ item.label }}">{{ item.label }}</span>
      <button type="button"
        data-option-picker-chip-remove
        class="shrink-0 text-text-faint hover:text-text focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus-ring"
        aria-label="Remove {{ item.label }} from {{ field_name|default('selection') }}">
        {{ include('bb_theme:icon', { name: 'x-circle', size: 'sm' }, with_context = false) }}
      </button>
    </span>
    {%- endfor %}
  </span>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if autosave %}
  <span id="{{ picker_id }}__status" data-picker-part="status" role="{{ invalid ? 'alert' : 'status' }}" class="empty:hidden {{ use_chips ? '' : 'ml-inline' }} text-meta {{ invalid ? 'text-state-attention-ink' : 'text-text-light' }}">{{ status }}</span>
  {%- endif %}
  {#- Variant alignment is the no-JS default; the behavior fits open menus to the viewport. #}
  <div id="{{ panel }}"
    data-picker-part="panel" class="absolute top-full mt-1.5 {{ is_inline ? 'right-0' : 'left-0' }} z-30 w-max min-w-66 max-w-90 max-h-70 overflow-y-auto bg-surface-2 border border-border rounded-sm p-1.5 shadow-shadow-2"
    data-option-picker-panel
    x-ref="panel"
    :hidden="!open"
    {#- The delegated panel click the behaviour used to register: one listener
        on the panel, resolving the clicked row with `closest()`. #}
    @click="$event.target.closest('[role=\'option\']') && pick($event.target.closest('[role=\'option\']'))"
    @keydown="keydown($event)"
    {%- if not open %} hidden{% endif %}>
    {%- if searchable %}
    <div data-picker-part="search" class="mb-1.5">
      {{ include('bb_theme:form_input', {
        type: 'search',
        placeholder: search_placeholder|default('Search'),
        attributes: search_input_attributes,
      }, with_context = false) }}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if search_url %}<div id="{{ panel }}__rows" data-picker-part="rows">{% endif %}
    {% block options %}{% if options %}{{ options }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}
    {%- if search_url %}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {#- The field variant writes when the FORM does, so the picked values ride along
      as hidden inputs. The inline variant deliberately emits none: the pick is
      the write, so there is no form to submit them with. #}
  {%- if not is_inline and name %}
    {%- for selected_value in values|default([]) %}
  <input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}{{ multiple ? '[]' : '' }}" value="{{ selected_value }}" />
    {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
</div>
